# GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj (CVE-2026-33327, CVE-2026-33328, CVE-2026-35590, CVE-2026-35591)
# libvips vulnerabilities inherited by sharp, bundled as an optionalDependency of next@16.2.x.
# next@16.2.x pins sharp@^0.34.5 — npm overrides do not apply to optionalDependencies and
# no updated Next.js release is available. sharp is used for static image optimisation only
# (not processing user-supplied data), so the attack surface is minimal.
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
CVE-2026-33327
CVE-2026-33328
CVE-2026-35590
CVE-2026-35591

# CVE-2026-64641, CVE-2026-64642, CVE-2026-64645, CVE-2026-64649: Next.js App Router vulnerabilities.
# Affected package: next@16.2.6 (fixed in 16.2.11).
# CVE-2026-64641: DoS via Server Actions — requires Server Actions exposed to untrusted input.
# CVE-2026-64642: Middleware bypass — requires Turbopack, which is not enabled in this project.
# CVE-2026-64645: SSRF via rewrites — this application does not use rewrites with external
# destinations.
# CVE-2026-64649: SSRF in Server Actions on custom servers — this project uses Next.js standalone
# mode (not a custom server). Upgrade to next@16.2.11 is planned for the next sprint.
CVE-2026-64641
CVE-2026-64642
CVE-2026-64645
CVE-2026-64649

# CVE-2026-45623, GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849: PostCSS file read / path traversal via sourceMappingURL.
# Affected package: postcss@8.4.31 bundled inside next@16.2.x (not a direct dependency).
# PostCSS is a build-time CSS processor; it is not executed at request time in the production
# image. CSS is compiled to static assets during `next build`; sourceMappingURL in user-supplied
# CSS is never processed at runtime. Will be resolved when next.js is upgraded to 16.2.11+.
CVE-2026-45623
GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849

# CVE-2025-47273: setuptools Path Traversal Vulnerability in PackageIndex.
# Affected package: setuptools==70.3.0 in the Debian base image system Python (/usr/local/lib).
# The venv and requirements.txt both pin setuptools==78.1.1 (patched). The system Python's
# setuptools is never invoked at runtime — the production container runs the Django app via the
# /venv Python and never executes `pip install`. CVE requires fetching packages from a malicious
# index, which cannot happen in a running container.
CVE-2025-47273

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964: msgpack Out-of-bounds read / crash on Unpacker reuse.
# Affected package: msgpack (indirect dependency of django-q2==1.7.2 which declares msgpack~=1.1).
# The venv installs msgpack==1.2.1 (patched); Trivy's detection is triggered by django-q2's package
# metadata listing msgpack~=1.1 as a dependency range — not by the actual runtime package.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# CVE-2026-23949: jaraco.context path traversal via malicious tar archives.
# CVE-2026-24049: wheel privilege escalation via malicious wheel files.
# Both affect vendor packages bundled inside setuptools/_vendor/ (jaraco.context==5.3.0,
# wheel==0.45.1 shipped with setuptools==78.1.1). These code paths execute only during
# `pip install` — never at runtime in the production container.
# Fixed versions (jaraco.context>=6.1.0, wheel>=0.46.2) are not yet vendored by setuptools.
CVE-2026-23949
CVE-2026-24049
